      "description": "<p>Nasdaq erases 2026 gains and Asian markets record worst week since 2020 as investors question huge sums being poured into AI build-out</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/19/who-are-anthropic-founders\">Who are Anthropic’s seven co-founders, now worth $180bn?</a></p></li></ul><p>Anthropic’s shares fell at the start of its second day of trading, as its <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/19/anthropic-public-trading-ipo\">record-breaking IPO</a> failed to stem a sell-off in AI-linked companies.</p><p>As they dropped, the wider stock market fell with them, with the Nasdaq Composite erasing all its gains for 2026. The Dow Jones Industrial Average and S&amp;P 500 briefly entered correction territory.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/20/global-stock-markets-slump-anthropic-ipo-ai-sell-off\">Continue reading...</a>",
